// Package gen holds the Go types generated from the JSON schemas in the
// repository-level schemas/ directory, plus the raw schema documents used for
// runtime validation.
//
// Everything in this package except doc.go, register.go and their tests is
// generated by server/scripts/gen.sh ("make gen") and committed:
//
//   - <schema>_gen.go         types generated from schemas/<schema>.json
//   - <schema>_schema_gen.go  init() that registers the raw schema bytes
//
// Generated files are never edited by hand and never hand-written types are
// added here: change the schema, rerun the generator and commit the
// regenerated files together with the schema change. CI reruns the generator
// on a clean tree and fails on any diff (drift check).
//
// Schemas are looked up by file name without the .json extension ("core",
// "pi", "ws", ...) and must produce unique type names across files, because
// every generated file lands in this single package.
//
// A schema that has no generated file yet is simply absent: SchemaJSON reports
// (nil, false) and Schemas omits it. Callers must degrade gracefully instead
// of assuming a schema exists, so a partial schemas/ directory never breaks a
// build.
package gen
